# Always run commands yourself

Shashank is busy. **You run every command** — do not ask him to paste, install, convert, or “run this in the terminal.”

## Do

- Use the Shell tool (and other tools) for installs, builds, typecheck, git, `gh`, PDF/DOCX extract, screenshots, scrapes, tests, deploys.
- Install missing local tools/packages yourself when needed for the task (`pip`, `npm`, CLI helpers).
- If Auto-review / Smart Mode blocks a command that is required for the task, **retry immediately** with approval (`request_smart_mode_approval`) — do not stop and ask him to run it.
- For attached PDFs, DOCX, images, or Downloads paths: extract/read them yourself, then answer.
- Prefer parallel tool calls when gathering evidence.

## Do not

- Say “run this locally” / “please execute” / “you can run…” for work you can do in the agent shell.
- Dump a command block and wait for him to run it (unless a step truly needs his browser/UI only — e.g. reload Chrome extension, click Approve once).
- Skip investigation because a command “might need approval.”

## Allowed exceptions (him only)

- Chrome extension reload at `chrome://extensions`
- One-click UI approval cards the agent cannot click
- Secrets he must paste into a dashboard (never ask him to run git/npm for that)

## Example

```text
❌ “Convert the PDF to images and paste them here”
✅ Rasterize/OCR/extract with Shell, then review

❌ “Run npm run typecheck”
✅ Run `npm run typecheck` yourself and report the result
```
